Data Subject Access Request Workflow Automation
Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Deploy a local ticketing system to intake DSAR requests
Create structured DSAR templates for access, deletion, and portability rights
Implement OTP-based identity verification using local SMTP
Build a script to generate JSON data portability bundles from a database
Track SLA compliance timers and generate a compliance report
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command-line skills (file editing, permissions, package management)
Basic Python 3 knowledge (functions, JSON, file I/O)
Basic SQL/SQLite familiarity
Understanding of GDPR data subject rights (Access, Rectification, Erasure, Portability)
Familiarity with Docker is helpful but not required
Environment Setup
Single Linux machine (Ubuntu 22.04+) provided via Start Lab
Install required packages:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose python3 python3-pip sqlite3 mailutils
sudo systemctl start docker
pip3 install pyotp
Task 1: Set Up Local Ticketing System
Zammad requires significant resources; for this lab we use a lightweight alternative — Django-based ticket simulator via a local SQLite-backed Flask app (faster to provision, same workflow concepts).

Create project directory:
mkdir -p ~/dsar-lab/{tickets,scripts,templates,reports}
cd ~/dsar-lab
Create the ticket intake database schema:
sqlite3 tickets/dsar.db <<EOF
CREATE TABLE requests (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  subject_email TEXT NOT NULL,
  request_type TEXT NOT NULL,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'received',
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  sla_deadline TIMESTAMP,
  verified INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);
EOF
